# Agent instructions

## Search and read

When the current project is a git repository, use the basemind MCP server for file name and content search before reaching for shell tools.

- Locate a file by name: `basemind` code mode `find`.
- Search file contents: `basemind` code mode `grep`.
- Read a file: code mode `outline` first, then `expand` for the one symbol you need.
- History and blame: basemind `git` modes instead of `git log`, `git blame`, `git diff`.
- PDFs, markdown, JSON, YAML, TOML: `memory` mode `documents`.

Outside a repository, basemind has no index. Use the shell there.

After edits, run the basemind `admin` mode `rescan` so new symbols are searchable.
